
Property set operations.
USAGE:

SET <assign list>
NOTE: <assign list> can be more than one property name separated by commas.
Each property name should be followed by '=' and its value.

The following writeable properties are available:
Property				Type			Operation
========				====			=========
ASPScriptDefaultNamespace          	string              	Read/Write
ASPScriptEnabled                   	boolean             	Read/Write
AutoStartWin9X                     	uint32              	Read/Write
BackupInterval                     	uint32              	Read/Write
BackupLastTime                     	datetime            	Read/Write
EnableAnonWin9xConnections         	boolean             	Read/Write
EnableEvents                       	boolean             	Read/Write
EnableStartupHeapPreallocation     	boolean             	Read/Write
HighThresholdOnClientObjects       	uint32              	Read/Write
HighThresholdOnEvents              	uint32              	Read/Write
LoggingDirectory                   	string              	Read/Write
LoggingLevel                       	uint32              	Read/Write
LowThresholdOnClientObjects        	uint32              	Read/Write
LowThresholdOnEvents               	uint32              	Read/Write
MaxLogFileSize                     	uint32              	Read/Write
MaxWaitOnClientObjects             	uint32              	Read/Write
MaxWaitOnEvents                    	uint32              	Read/Write

